From 1ca92b8ad94e0d8e9f244cc6810273041bda0f10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Ceccarelli Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 03:17:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v11): machine control and software integration

The layer where software becomes machine behaviour, with the budget that
decides whether it holds.

- lib/control.ts: loop dead-time budget (ZOH + sensor + transport +
  compute + actuator), phase lag phi = 360*f*Td, achievable closed-loop
  bandwidth inverted from a chosen phase budget, sample-rate adequacy
  against the 10-20x rule; plus fieldbus frame time, bus utilisation,
  axes that fit a cycle and the fastest cycle an axis count supports.
  Verified by hand: 1 kHz loop with 700 us transport gives 1.2 ms dead
  time and 69.4 Hz at a 30 deg budget, and the phase-lag round trip
  closes exactly on the budget.
- /tools/control-loop-calculator (en + de): both budgets, verdict codes
  for marginal sampling, delay-dominated architecture, compute overrun,
  dead time exceeding a period, and bus over-capacity.
- /disciplines/control-integration (en + de): determinism and bounded
  worst-case timing, motion profiles and kinematics, fieldbus budgets,
  state machines and diagnostics, and the agentic layer above them.

The safety boundary is stated on both pages and is not negotiable: an
agent may interpret, propose, explain and generate; it may not close a
cycle-time-critical loop and may never implement a safety function.
Safety-rated stopping, speed and separation monitoring, interlocks and
emergency stop belong on qualified hardware under their own standards.

